Time complexity analysis:

Iterating over a list to create the linked list is O(n) due to having to append each of the n items onto the list. Removing the duplicates by iterating through the linked list is also O(n) because you have to check and possibly remove each of the n items. Therefore, the total time complexity is O(n + n) which simplifies to O(n).

Space complexity analysis:

The space complexity of the solution is also O(n), where n is the number of items in the list. This is because in the worst case scenario, a new linked list node is created for each item in the list, and a new entry is created in the set for each unique item.

