```

This function data_structure_identifier takes an object (data structure instance) as input and returns the name of the data structure, the category and its brief description. Data structure category 'Scalar' comprises of Linear and Hierarchical type data structures like Linked List, Binary Tree etc. 'Array' category compromises of sequential Array type data structures like List, Tuple etc and 'Hash' category is for Map or Set type data structures like Dictionary, Set etc. Please note, we are interpreting HashMap as 'Hash' not its traditional 'Array' interpretation as it's in Python implemented as a 'Hash' table. The function returns 'Unknown Data Structure', 'Unknown Category' for unknown types.

