#include<iostream>
#include<cmath>
#include<climits>

// Function to safely convert a long double to a short int.
short safeConvert(long double d)
{
    // Check if the value of d is within the limit of short int.
    if(d < SHRT_MIN || d > SHRT_MAX)
    {
        std::cout << "Error: the value " << d << " exceeds the range of a short int." << '\n';
        return 0;
    }

    // Calculate the fractional part of d and 0.5.
    long double delta = d - std::trunc(d);
    short result;

    // If the fractional part of d is less than 0.5, round down the number. Otherwise, round up.
    if(delta < 0.5)
        result = (short)std::floor(d);
    else
        result = (short)std::ceil(d);

    // Check if the original double d and the converted short result can match exactly. If they cannot match exactly, output a warning.
    if(result != d)
        std::cout << "Warning: Rounding occurred when converting " << d << " to a short int." << '\n';

    return result;
}

int main()
{
    std::cout << "Please input a long double number : ";
    long double d;
    if(!(std::cin >> d))
    {
        std::cout << "Error: Invalid input! A number was expected." << '\n';
        return 1;
    }
    short int si = safeConvert(d);
    std::cout << "The short int is : " << si << '\n';
    return 0;
}
```

This program includes a function to safely convert a long double to a short int. First, the program checks whether the input is within the range of a short int. If the number is out range, the program gives an error message. The program uses mathematical operations to round the long double number: if the fractional part of the long double number is less than 0.5, the program rounds down the number. Otherwise, it rounds up. The program then checks whether the original long double number and the resulted short int match exactly. If there is not an exact match, the program gives a warning message. In the main function, the program gets the input from the user and checks whether the input is numeric. If the input is not valid, the program gives an error message.

