Here is a simple JavaScript function which takes a string input and uses regular expressions to determine if the string is numerical (either in decimal or hexadecimal form). The function first checks if the string begins with '0x', if yes, then it checks if the rest of the string is in valid hexadecimal format. If the string does not begin with '0x', it checks if the string is a regular numerical value.

```javascript
function isNumericOrHexadecimal(s) {
    const hexadecimalRegEx = /^0x[0-9a-fA-F]+$/;
    const numericRegEx = /^[0-9]+$/;

    if (s.startsWith('0x')) {
        return hexadecimalRegEx.test(s);
    } else {
        return numericRegEx.test(s);
    }
}
```

This function will return `true` if the input string is either a numerical value, or a valid hexadecimal value (starting with '0x'). It will return `false` if the input string is neither.

