1. Backend architecture
Python Flask is a lightweight web server framework that's great for small to medium applications. We will extend it with Flask-SocketIO to get WebSocket support.

```python
from flask import Flask, render_template
from flask_socketio import SocketIO, emit

app = Flask(__name__)
socketio = SocketIO(app)

@socketio.on('message')
def handle_message(message):
    emit('message', message, broadcast=True)

if __name__ == '__main__':
    socketio.run(app, host='0.0.0.0', port=5000)
```
In this script, Flask app is initialized and so is SocketIO with the app as a parameter. The `@socketio.on('message')` decorator creates an event listener for 'message' events, broadcast= True ensure the message is sent to all clients connected to the WebSocket.

