3. WebSockets role and potential challenges

WebSockets provide a full-duplex communication protocol over a single, long-lived connection. It allows server and clients to communicate in real-time with low latency. However, WebSocket connections aren't immune to errors and disconnections. 

Handling Connection Errors & Reconnections: Socket.IO does a good job of handling disconnections and reconnections. In fact, by default, it will reconnect automatically.

Handling Binary Data: The default data types that can be sent through WebSockets are text (UTF-8) and binary (Blob, ArrayBuffer, and ArrayBufferView). For sending binary data, you can just emit it like:

```javascript
var blob = new Blob(["hello, world"]);
socket.emit('message', blob);
```

