We first filter out the alphanumeric characters from the string. Then, for every alphabetic character we increment its ASCII value and make sure it cycles within the a-z or A-Z range (the ASCII values of 'z' and 'Z' should wrap around to 'a' and 'A' respectively). Finally, we sort the resulting characters in lexicographic order and join them into a single string:

```python
def encrypt_and_order(text):
    res = ''
    for ch in text:
        if ch.isalpha():
            if ch.islower():
                res += chr((ord(ch) - 96) % 26 + 97)
            else:
                res += chr((ord(ch) - 65) % 26 + 65)
    return ''.join(sorted(res))

