```

The `solve` function uses the `fetch` function in a `try...catch` block for error handling. If the `fetch` operation fails (for example, if the URL does not exist), the error will be caught and logged. Finally, it returns an object that contains an array of internal links and an array of external links. Each link in the external array includes the HTTP status code, so you can see if it's active or not.

