The 'new' function is a constructor that creates a new node.

The 'insert' function is used to insert a new value into the tree. If the new value is bigger than the current node's value, it's inserted into the right subtree; otherwise, it's inserted into the left subtree.

The 'in_order_traversal' function traverses the binary tree in-order (visiting the left subtree, then the root node, then the right subtree), and applies a callback function to each visited node.

The 'tree_sort' function creates a binary search tree from the input vector and then uses in-order traversal to retrieve the values in ascending order.

