```
This will generate a 2x2x2 tensor filled with distinct random integers between 0 and 10.

This is an improved version. It uses a binary search algorithm with recursion to find the user's input in a predefined sorted array. It also validates the user's input ensuring that it is a number and within the array. If the input is invalid, it prompts the user to input again.

```java
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.InputMismatchException;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Specify a pre-defined sorted array for lookup
        int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 6, 8, 13, 18, 27, 34, 41, 50};

        System.out.println("Enter the target number: ");
        while (!input.hasNextInt()) {
            System.out.println("Invalid input. Please enter a number: ");
            input.next();
        }
        int target = input.nextInt();

        int result = binarySearch(arr, 0, arr.length - 1, target);
        if (result == -1) {
            System.out.println("Number not found in array, try again");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Number found at index " + result);
        }
    }

    public static int binarySearch(int[] array, int left, int right, int target) {
        if (right >= left) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            // If the middle element is our goal
            if (array[mid] == target)
                return mid;

            // If the middle element is greater than the goal
            // We can only use the left side (mid - 1) of the array
            if (array[mid] > target)
                return binarySearch(array, left, mid - 1, target);

            // Else, we can only use the right side (mid + 1) of the array
            return binarySearch(array, mid + 1, right, target);
        }

        // We reach here when the element is not present in the array
        return -1;
    }
}
```
This programs expects user to input a number, if not it will keep asking until user provides valid number. Then it uses the Binary Search algorithm to find if number exists in the predefined array. If it exists, it returns the index position, otherwise it informs the user that number is not found in the array.

