在Java中，我們可以編寫一個函數來實現泡沫排序算法。這個函數將從數字陣列的開始處開始工作，將每一對相鄰的數字進行比較，如果前一個數字比後面那個數字大，那麼這個函數就會交換它們的位置。這個過程會一直重複，直到函數遍歷過整個陣列而沒有進行任何交換為止。這意味著數組已經完全排序了。

以下是實現泡沫排序的Java程式碼：

```java
public class BubbleSortExample {  
    static void bubbleSort(int[] arr) {  
        int n = arr.length;  
        int temp = 0;  
         for(int i=0; i < n; i++){  
                 for(int j=1; j < (n-i); j++){  
                          if(arr[j-1] > arr[j]){  
                                 //swap elements  
                                 temp = arr[j-1];  
                                 arr[j-1] = arr[j];  
                                 arr[j] = temp;  
                         }  

                 }  
         }  

    }  
    public static void main(String[] args) {  
                int arr[] ={3,60,35,2,45,320,5,12,15,10};  

                System.out.println("Array Before Bubble Sort");  
                for(int i=0; i < arr.length; i++){  
                        System.out.print(arr[i] + " ");  
                }  
                System.out.println();  

                bubbleSort(arr);//sorting array elements using bubble sort  

                System.out.println("Array After Bubble Sort");  
                for(int i=0; i < arr.length; i++){  
                        System.out.print(arr[i] + " ");  
                }  

        }  
}
```

這個程式在開始時會先定義一個包含10個整數的陣列，然後它會用`System.out.println`函數來列印出未排序以及排序完成後的陣列。

Here is the simple Java program to check if a given string is palindrome:

```Java
public class PalindromeChecker {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String str = "racecar";
        if(isPalindrome(str)){
            System.out.println(str + " is a palindrome");
        }else{
            System.out.println(str + " is not a palindrome");
        }
    }

    public static boolean isPalindrome(String str) {
        int i = 0, j = str.length() -1;

        while(i < j) {
            if(str.charAt(i) != str.charAt(j)) {
                return false;
            }
            i++;
            j--;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```
This above program works by comparing the first and the last characters of the string. Then, the second character and the second last character and so on until the middle of the string is reached. If, at any point, the characters being compared are not equal, the function returns false indicating that the string is not a palindrome. If all pairs of characters match, then the string is a palindrome.

You can replace `"racecar"` with other word/string to check whether it is a palindrome or not.

