Creating a RESTful API endpoint involves defining URLs to perform different actions (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE) on resources (customers in this case). This example demonstrates how to create a RESTful API end point that lists all customers using the Node.js framework, Express.js. We'll use a hypothetical CustomerModel which is an interface to the customer database.

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const router = express.Router();

// This would be your actual model interfacing with the database
const CustomerModel = require('../models/customer');

// GET request to /api/customers
router.get('/api/customers', async (req, res) => {
    try {
        // Query the database for all customers
        const customers = await CustomerModel.getAll();

        // if customers found, return them with status 200
        if (customers.length > 0) {
            res.status(200).json(customers);
        } 
        // else send status 404 (not found)
        else {
            res.status(404).json({ message: "No customers found." });
