Here is a simple example of a Java program that uses threading and takes console-based input. In the following code, two threads are created - one for reading user input, and another for processing that input. The `ProcessorThread` only starts processing the input after the `ReaderThread` has finished reading.

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Data data = new Data();
        Thread readerThread = new Thread(new ReaderThread(data));
        Thread processorThread = new Thread(new ProcessorThread(data));

        readerThread.start();
        processorThread.start();
    }
}

class Data {
    private String value;
    private boolean isProcessed = true;

    public synchronized void readValue() {
        if (!isProcessed) {
            try {
                wait();
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Enter a text: ");
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        this.value = scanner.nextLine();
        isProcessed = false;
        notifyAll();
    }

    public synchronized void processValue() {
        if (isProcessed) {
            try {
                wait();
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                e.printStackTrace();
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Entered text: " + this.value);
        isProcessed = true;
        notifyAll();
    }
}

class ReaderThread implements Runnable {
    private Data data;

    public ReaderThread(Data data) {
        this.data = data;
    }

    @Override
    public void run() {
        while (true) {
            data.readValue();
        }
    }
}

class ProcessorThread implements Runnable {
    private Data data;

    public ProcessorThread(Data data) {
        this.data = data;
    }

    @Override
    public void run() {
        while (true) {
            data.processValue();
        }
    }
}
```

The possible flawed version of the code is as follows:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Data data = new Data();
        Thread readerThread = new Thread(new ReaderThread(data));
        Thread processorThread = new Thread(new ProcessorThread(data));

