console.log(regexMatch(123456)); // Output: Non-string inputs are not accepted
``` 

This `regexMatch` function first checks that the input is a string. If not, it throws an error. Then checks if the string is empty, then checks if the string contains only numeric characters via a regex match. Finally it counts the number of even digits in the string, assuming that it has passed all previous checks, and returns the result. If at any point a condition fails, it will return an appropriate error message.

