在JavaScript中，解決這個問題的一種方法是使用一個字典或者哈希表來跟蹤每個字元的出現次數。如果字串可以形成回文，那麼最多只會有一個字元的出現次數是奇數。

以下是一個代碼範例：

```javascript
function canFormPalindrome(str) {
    let charOccurrences = new Map();

    // 計算每個字元的出現次數
    for(let char of str) {
        if(charOccurrences.has(char)) {
            charOccurrences.set(char, charOccurrences.get(char)+1);
        } else {
            charOccurrences.set(char, 1);
        }
    }

    let oddCount = 0;
    // 檢查最多只有一個字元的出現次數是奇數
    for(let count of charOccurrences.values()){
        if(count % 2 !== 0){
            oddCount++;
        }
        if(oddCount > 1){
            return false;
        }
    }

    // 如果沒有返回false，則返回true
    return true;
}

console.log(canFormPalindrome("cArerAc")); // 輸出: true
console.log(canFormPalindrome("#$$#")); // 輸出: true
```
這個函式首先計算出給定字串中每個字元的出現次數。然後，它檢查字串中是否有多於一個出現次數為奇數的字元。如果有，那麼該字串不能形成回文，函式返回 false。否則，函式返回 true。

該解決方案的時間複雜度為O(n), 其中n為給定字串的長度。因為函式中的每個操作（包括對給定字串中的每個字元的迭代，以及計算和檢查每個字元出現次數）都是在固定時間內完成的。其空間複雜度也為O(n)，因為需要存儲給定字串中每個字元的出現次數。

You can implement the `MapSum` class using two HashMaps. The first map will hold the key value pair and the second map will hold every prefix and suffix of keys with the cumulative sum of their corresponding values. Here is a Java solution. 

```java
class MapSum {
    HashMap<String, Integer> map;
    HashMap<String, Integer> score;
    public MapSum() {
        map = new HashMap();
        score = new HashMap();
    }

    public void insert(String key, int val) {
        if (!map.containsKey(key)) {
            for (int i = 0; i <= key.length(); ++i) {
                String prefix = key.substring(0, i);
                score.put(prefix, score.getOrDefault(prefix, 0) + val);
            }
            for (int i = 0; i <= key.length(); ++i) {
                String suffix = key.substring(key.length() - i);
                score.put(suffix, score.getOrDefault(suffix, 0) + val);
            }
        } else {
            int delta = val - map.get(key);
            for (int i = 0; i <= key.length(); ++i) {
                String prefix = key.substring(0, i);
                score.put(prefix, score.get(prefix) + delta);
            }
            for (int i = 0; i <= key.length(); ++i) {
                String suffix = key.substring(key.length() - i);
                score.put(suffix, score.get(suffix) + delta);
            }
        }
        map.put(key, val);
    }

    public int sum(String prefix) {
        return score.getOrDefault(prefix, 0);
    }

    public int sumSuffix(String suffix) {
        return score.getOrDefault(suffix,0);
    }
}
```

The `insert` method first checks whether the given key is already present in the map or not. If it is not present, then it simply adds all the prefixes and suffixes of the key with the value `val`. If the key is already present then it calculates the difference between the new value and the old value and adds the difference to the prefix and suffix. The `sum` method simply returns the sum of all values whose keys start with the given prefix and `sumSuffix` returns the sum of all values whose keys end with the given suffix. If the provided prefix/suffix does not exist, it returns 0.

