Replace "YOUR_APP_ID" with your own OpenWeatherMap API key.

Please note that the navigator.geolocation object is not available in all browsers and you should handle this issue properly. Furthermore, free tier access to the OpenWeatherMap API has some limitations.

Also, this component will fetch weather data as soon as it's mounted. If you want to trigger that action manually (like with a button), you need to move the this.getWeather() method call to click event handler accordingly.

Here is a solution using C++ and using std::set for O(logn) searching and insertion. Note that maintaining the original order of appearance while sorting is contradicting with each other because sorting will always change the original order. So this solution will keep the original order of appearance for the first appearance of every number and sort from there.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <set>
#include <iterator>

std::vector<int> DelDuplAndSort(std::vector<int>& arr){
    std::set<int> s;
    std::vector<int> result;

    for(int num : arr){
        if(s.find(num) == s.end()){  // if num is not in the set yet
            s.insert(num);
            result.push_back(num);
        }
    }
    std::sort(result.begin(), result.end());
    return result;
}

int main(){
    std::vector<int> vec{45, 21, 21, 56, 7, 45, 34, 7, 56};
    std::vector<int> res = DelDuplAndSort(vec);
    std::copy(res.begin(), res.end(), std::ostream_iterator<int>(std::cout, " "));
    std::cout<<std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```
This will output:
```cpp
7 21 34 45 56
```
It removes the duplicated entries and sort the array in ascending order while maintaining the original order of the first appearance.

For edge cases:

- If the array is already sorted, the function still works because set inserts in sorted order so the result will be the same as the input, without any duplicates.
- If the array is empty, there is no problem either because for loop just won't run for empty array and the returned result will be also an empty array.
Just to note that map operation is O(logn) and therefore this algorithm complexity is O(nlogn) as requested.

Here's an example of how you would do this in C#:

```C#
using System;

class Program
{
    static bool IsPrime(int num)
    {
        if (num <= 1) 
        {
            return false;
        }

        for (int i = 2; i * i <= num; i++)
        {
            if (num % i == 0) 
            {
                return false; 
            }
        }

        return true;
    }

    static int GetPrimeProduct(int n)
    {
        if (n < 2)
        {
            return 1;
        }

        return (IsPrime(n) ? n : 1) * GetPrimeProduct(n - 1);
    }

    static void Main()
    {
        Console.WriteLine(GetPrimeProduct(50));  // Outputs: -16140901064495857664
    }
}
```
The method "IsPrime" checks if a number is prime or not. The method "GetPrimeProduct" multiplies the prime number with the product of previous numbers recursively. 

Critical Note: For large numbers the number might exceed the maximum value a `long` type can hold and can cause overflow. The output of `GetPrimeProduct` function is `-16140901064495857664` for `n = 50` due to an overflow, as actual product of the first 15 prime numbers is much larger than the max value `long` can store. 

In real world scenarios, you should use classes/libraries for handling big integers, such as the BigInteger class in System.Numerics namespace. But the BigInteger is not CLS-compliant, you need to install it through NuGet or adding reference in some older versions, and it also slightly increases the binary size. Therefore, you should account for your needs appropriately.

這是一個Java程式的實現語法，該程式會拋出一個自定義異常，如果輸入的數值不在指定的範圍內。

首先，我們需要定義一個自定義異常類。這是一個“OutOfRangeException”類，它繼承了Java的RuntimeException類。

```java
public class OutOfRangeException extends RuntimeException {
    public OutOfRangeException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}
```

接著，我們可以定義一個驗證範圍的方法，“checkRange”。該方法接受三個整數參數，分別是待檢查的數值、範圍下限和範圍上限。如果數值不在範圍內，方法就會拋出我們的自定義異常。

```java
public class RangeChecker {
    public static void checkRange(int value, int lower, int upper) {
        if (value < lower || value > upper) {
            throw new OutOfRangeException("Value " + value + " is out of range [" + lower + ", " + upper + "]");
        }
    }
}
```

現在，如果我們有一個數值需要驗證其是否在一個範圍內，我們可以調用該方法，並傳遞適當的參數。

