To create a Java program that outputs the Fibonacci sequence up to a specified integer value, you can use a loop to generate the series iteratively. Here's an example of a Java program that implements this functionality:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class FibonacciSequence {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter a positive integer value to calculate the Fibonacci sequence up to: ");
        int maxNumber = scanner.nextInt();
        scanner.close();

        if (maxNumber <= 0) {
            System.out.println("Please input a positive number.");
        } else {
            System.out.printf("Fibonacci sequence up to %d is:%n", maxNumber);
            int num1 = 0;
            int num2 = 1;

            while (num1 <= maxNumber) {
                // Print the number
                System.out.print(num1 + " ");

                // Calculate the next number in the sequence
                int nextNumber = num1 + num2;

                // Update num1 as num2 and num2 as the next number in the sequence
                num1 = num2;
                num2 = nextNumber;
            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }
}
```

