StackOverflow! and overflowStack!: False
@dVent!ONera and oneRAadVENT!@: True
```

Time complexity analysis:
Let n be the length of the longest string. The time complexity of the algorithm is O(n) because it traverses each string once. Note that creating and updating the hash map is a constant time operation, thus it does not affect the overall time complexity.

Thus, the algorithm is quite efficient and can handle even big strings effectively. However, it assumes that all strings can fit in memory. If this is not the case, then using a hash map would not be feasible, and we would need to consider a different approach.

