```php
<?php
// Your array
$arr = array(13, 62, 17, 41, 32, 27, 89);

// Sort the array
sort($arr);

// Count the number of items in the array
$n = count($arr);

// Check if the count is even or odd
if ($n % 2 == 0) {
    // If even, calculate the average of the two middle numbers
    $midpoint1 = $arr[$n / 2];
    $midpoint2 = $arr[($n / 2) - 1];
    $median = ($midpoint1 + $midpoint2) / 2;
} else {
    // If odd, the median is the middle number
    $median = $arr[floor($n / 2)];
}

echo $median;
?>
```
This script works by first sorting the array in ascending order. If the count of items in the array is even, it calculate the average of the two middle numbers. If it is odd, the median is simply the middle number.

