這是一個設計上相對複雜的問題，但並不意味著我們不能解決。我們首先需要處理字符串輸入，然後根據閏年和正常年分別定義月份，並計算出具有多少天。然後，我們的任務就是進行準確的減法運算以獲得準確的年齡。

以下是一種可能的解決方案：

```javascript
function calculateAge(birthdate) {
  const dateParts = birthdate.split("-");
  const year = parseInt(dateParts[0]);
  const month = parseInt(dateParts[1]);
  const day = parseInt(dateParts[2]);

  const today = new Date();
  const todayYear = today.getFullYear();
  const todayMonth = today.getMonth() + 1; // In JS months start from 0
  const todayDay = today.getDate();

  let ageYear = todayYear - year;
  if (todayMonth < month || (todayMonth == month && todayDay < day)) {
    ageYear--;
  }

  let ageMonth = todayMonth - month;
  if (todayMonth < month) {
    ageMonth += 12;
  }
  if (todayDay < day) {
    ageMonth--;
  }

  let ageDay = todayDay - day;
  if (todayDay < day) {
    const isLeapYear = todayYear % 400 === 0 || (todayYear % 100 !== 0 && todayYear %4 === 0);
    const daysInMonth = [31, (isLeapYear ? 29 : 28), 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31]
    ageDay += daysInMonth[(todayMonth - 2 + 12) % 12];
  }

  return {
    years: ageYear,
    months: ageMonth,
    days: ageDay
  };
}
```
注意上述代碼使用了JavaScript的內建Date類型。如果不希望使用，可以自己獲取當前時間。留意於準確地處理閏年和非閏年的每個月的天數。

Here is a solution using Kadane's algorithm (assumed you want to find the max sum):

```cpp
#include<iostream>
#include<vector>
#include<climits>
using namespace std;

int findMaxSubArraySum(vector<int> &nums) {
    int max_so_far = INT_MIN, max_ending_here = 0;

    for (int i = 0; i < nums.size(); i++)
    {
        max_ending_here = max_ending_here + nums[i];
        if (max_so_far < max_ending_here)
            max_so_far = max_ending_here;

        if (max_ending_here < 0)
            max_ending_here = 0;
    }

    return max_so_far;
}

int main()
{
    vector<int> nums = {-2, -3, 4, -1, -2, 1, 5, -3};
    int max_sum = findMaxSubArraySum(nums);
    cout << "Maximum contiguous sum of subarray is: " << max_sum;
    return 0;
}
```

This program will display the sum of the largest contiguous sub-array within the given array of integers. The idea behind the Kadane's algorithm is simple. We initialize a variable `max_so_far` to INT_MIN and `max_ending_here` to 0, and then iterate over the array. For each element, we update `max_ending_here` to `max_ending_here + nums[i]` and update `max_so_far` if `max_ending_here` is greater than `max_so_far`. If `max_ending_here` becomes less than 0, then we reset `max_ending_here` to 0.

Finally, `max_so_far` will hold the sum of the largest contiguous sub-array. Please note that Kadane's algorithm doesn't work if all the elements of the array are negative as it at least needs a non-negative number to work correctly.

