    name: "John",
    age: 30,
    cars: {
        car1: "Ford",
        car2: "BMW",
        car3: "Fiat"
    }
};

console.log(jsonToQueryString(json)); // outputs: name=John&age=30&cars[car1]=Ford&cars[car2]=BMW&cars[car3]=Fiat
```
In this example, a nested JSON object is passed to the function. The resulting string is printed to the console. Note that the nested objects have been flattened and encoded into a URL safe format.

