In this class, ArrayList is used to store the values. Since it is dynamic and can grow and shrink in size when values are added and removed respectively.

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class FloatCollection {

    private ArrayList<Float> values;

    public FloatCollection() {
        this.values = new ArrayList<Float>();
    }

    // Add value method
    public void addValue(float value) {
        this.values.add(value);
    }

    // Remove value method
    public void removeValue(float value) {
        this.values.remove(value);
    }

    // Get count method
    public int getCount() {
        return this.values.size();
    }

    // Calculate mean
    public float getMean() {
        float sum = 0;
        for(float value : values) {
            sum += value;
        }
        return sum/getCount();
    }

    // Calculate standard deviation
    public float getStdDev() {
        float mean = getMean();
        float temp = 0;
        for(float value : values) {
            temp += (mean-value)*(mean-value);
        }
        float variance = temp/getCount();
        return (float)Math.sqrt(variance);
    }
}
```

