The code terminates because the integer "i" eventually overflows and becomes negative after reaching its maximum value, interrupting the loop condition (i >= 0). 

In order to have an infinite loop, we can either not increment "i" or reset "i" in every loop cycle. Below are the corrected versions of the aforementioned code:

Option 1: not incrementing "i" 

```C++
#include<iostream>

