      <input type="text" value={input} onChange={handleChange} />
      <button onClick={handleClick}>Filter</button>
      {filteredArray.map((item, index) => (
        <p key={index}>{item.name}, {item.age}</p>
      ))}
    </div>
  )
}

export default App;
```

In this example, the state for the input field and filtered array is stored using the `useState` Hook. An event handler function `handleChange` is set for the input field that stores the user's input. The `handleClick` function is triggered when the button is clicked. In this function, the array is filtered to only contain items that include the user input. The filtered array is then set in the state and displayed in the render. The `toLowerCase()` function is used to make the search case-insensitive.

