To set up an AWS Lambda function to send automated emails, follow the below steps:

**1. Set up your AWS SES (Simple Email Service)**
Ensure that you have the verified email addresses or domains that you will use to send your email. 

**2. Set up your AWS Lambda Function**
Create a lambda function in your AWS console.

Click on the **"Create function"** button and fill in the details such as function name, runtime (Node.js 14.x) and choose an execution role that has AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole permission. This role allows your function to write logs to CloudWatch.

**3. Write your Lambda Function**

```javascript
// Initialize the Amazon SDK
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
AWS.config.update({region: 'us-west-2'});
const ses = new AWS.SES({apiVersion: '2010-12-01'});

exports.handler = async (event) => {
    const message = JSON.parse(event.Records[0].Sns.Message);

    const EmailParams = {
        Destination: {
            ToAddresses: message.recipientEmails,
        },
        Message: {
            Body: {
                Text: {
                    Charset: "UTF-8",
                    Data: message.body,
                },
            },
            Subject: {
                Charset: 'UTF-8',
                Data: message.subject,
            },
        },
        Source: 'SENDER_EMAIL_ADDRESS',
    };

    try {
        const data = await ses.sendEmail(EmailParams).promise();
        console.log(data.MessageId);
    } catch (error) {
        console.error(error);
    }
};
```

Replace `'SENDER_EMAIL_ADDRESS'` with your own verified email address. 

Your JSON message would look similar to this:

```json
{
  "subject": "Hello from Lambda",
  "body": "This email was sent through AWS Lambda",
  "recipientEmails": ["recipient1@gmail.com", "recipient2@gmail.com"]
}
```

**4. Test Your Function**

