Sure, here is a function in C that calculates the Highest Common Factor (HCF), also known as the Greatest Common Divisor (GCD), of two numbers. 

```c
#include <stdio.h>

// Function to compute the Highest Common Factor
int gcd(int a, int b){
    if (b == 0)
        return a;
    else
        return gcd(b, a % b);
}

int main(){
    int num1 = 528, num2 = 396;

    printf("The HCF of %d and %d is %d.", num1, num2, gcd(num1, num2));
    return 0;
}
```

This code uses the Euclidean algorithm to calculate the gcd/HCF. This mathematical algorithm works on the principle that the gcd of two numbers a and b is the same as the gcd of b and the remainder of a divided by b. The algorithm is applied recursively until the second number becomes 0, at which point the first number is returned as the gcd.

