This script defines a `ComputedGrammar` class that will generate a Context Free Grammar (CFG) from a Regular Expression (regex). The `generateCFG` method scans the regex from left to right. For each `|` and `*` in the regex, it appends a new production rule `Tn`, where `n` is a incremented counter. The rest of the characters are simply appended as terminals.

In the `main` function, it prompts the user to input a regex. This regex is then fed into the `generateCFG` method from a `ComputedGrammar` instance. The resulting CFG is then printed out to the console.

Please note, conversion from regex to CFG can be a complex process and might not be perfect in all cases (especially for exotic regex). It's suggested to use parsers (like ANTLR, etc.) for production ready conversion.

