First, let's implement the custom method tocalculate the square root of a number. A common method to find the square root of a number is using binary search, which has a time complexity of O(log n). 

```java
public class SquareRoot {
    // Static epsilon describes the precision of our calculations
    private static final double EPSILON = 1e-6;

    public static double squareRoot(double num) {
        // Return -1 for negative numbers 
        if (num < 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Number should be non-negative");
        }

        double low = 0;
        double high = num;

        // Handling edge case of num<1
        if(num<1){
            low = num;
            high = 1;
        }

        while ((high - low) > EPSILON) {
            double mid = (high + low) / 2;
            if (mid * mid > num) {
                high = mid;
            } else {
                low = mid;
            }
        }
        return low;
    }
}
```

