Below is a java solution for the problem. It generates a randomized 4x4 array between 1 and 16 and checks if its a magic square:


```java
import java.util.Arrays;
import java.util.Random;

public class MagicSquare {
   private static final int SIZE = 4;
   private static final int MAX = SIZE * SIZE;

   public  static void main(String[] args){
       int[][] array = new int[SIZE][SIZE];
       boolean[] usedNumbers = new boolean[MAX + 1];
       Random random = new Random();

       for (int i = 0; i < SIZE; i++) {
           for (int j = 0; j < SIZE; j++){
               int num;
               do {
                   num = 1 + random.nextInt(MAX);
               }  while (usedNumbers[num]);
               usedNumbers[num] = true;
               array[i][j] = num;
               System.out.print(array[i][j] + " ");
           }
           System.out.println();
       }

       if (isMagicSquare(array)){
           System.out.println("The generated square is a magic square");
       } else {
           System.out.println("The generated square is not a magic square");
       }
   }

   private static boolean isMagicSquare(int[][] array) {
       int[] rowSum = new int[SIZE];
       int[] colSum = new int[SIZE];
       int[] diagSum = {0, 0};

       for (int i = 0; i < SIZE; i++) {
           for (int j = 0; j < SIZE; j++) {
               rowSum[i] += array[i][j];
               colSum[j] += array[i][j];
               if (i == j) {
                   diagSum[0] += array[i][j];
               }
               if (i == SIZE - j - 1) {
                   diagSum[1] += array[i][j];
               }
           }
       }

       for (int i = 1; i < SIZE; i++) {
           if (rowSum[i] != rowSum[i-1] || colSum[i] != colSum[i-1]) {
               return false;
           }
       }

       return diagSum[0] == diagSum[1] && diagSum[0] == rowSum[0] && diagSum[0] == colSum[0];
   }
}
```
This java program first generates a randomized 4x4 array with numbers 1 to 16, prints it out and then checks if it forms a magic square or not.

The `isMagicSquare` method checks if the provided 4x4 array forms a magic square or not. It calculates the sum of elements for each rows, columns and the 2 diagonals. If these sums are equal for all rows, columns and diagonals then it's a magic square otherwise not. 

Please note that generating a random 4x4 array does not increase your chances of getting a magic square. There are only a specific unique arrangements that make a magic square in 4x4 matrix which are hard to get randomly.

