```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String original = "Hello World!";
        reverseString(original);
    }

    private static void reverseString(String original) {
        char [] in = original.toCharArray();
        int begin = 0;
        int end = in.length - 1;
        char temp;

        while (end > begin) {
            temp = in[begin];
            in[begin] = in[end];
            in[end] = temp;
            end--;
            begin++;
        }

        System.out.println(new String(in));
    }
}
```

When run, this will print "!dlroW olleH", which is the reverse of "Hello World!". The `reverseString` method works by swapping characters at corresponding positions from the beginning and ending of the String. 

