Below is an implementation of a multithreaded Java program to search an element in a sorted 2D array utilizing binary search and divide and conquer strategy:

```java
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class MultiThreadedSearch {
    private int[][] matrix;
    private int target;
    private ExecutorService executor;

    public MultiThreadedSearch(int[][] matrix, int target) {
        this.matrix = matrix;
        this.target = target;
        this.executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4); // assuming a quad-core CPU
    }

    public boolean search() throws InterruptedException, ExecutionException {
        int rowCount = matrix.length;
        int colCount = matrix[0].length;
        Future<Boolean> result = null;

        for(int i=0; i<rowCount; i++) {
            final int row = i;
            result = executor.submit(() -> binarySearch(row, 0, colCount-1));
        }

        executor.shutdown();
        return result.get();
    }

    private boolean binarySearch(int row, int startIndex, int endIndex) {
        if(startIndex <= endIndex) {
            int midIndex = startIndex + (endIndex - startIndex) / 2;
            if(matrix[row][midIndex] == target) {
                return true;
            }
            if(matrix[row][midIndex] > target) {
                return binarySearch(row, startIndex, midIndex-1);
            }
            return binarySearch(row, midIndex+1, endIndex);
        }
        return false;
    }
}
```

