Here is a java code snippet that uses dynamic programming to find Fibonacci numbers and works for large numbers (upto the 1000th number in the sequence). It uses the BigInteger class in Java for handling large numbers:

```java
import java.math.BigInteger;

public class FibonacciDP {
    static BigInteger fib(int n) {
        // Array to store the fibonacci numbers
        BigInteger f[] = new BigInteger[n+1];
        f[0] = BigInteger.valueOf(0);
        f[1] = BigInteger.valueOf(1);

        // Fill remaining positions using the formula f[i] = f[i-1] + f[i-2]
        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++)
            f[i] = f[i-1].add(f[i-2]);

        return f[n];
    }

    public static void main (String args[]) {
        int n = 1000;
        System.out.println("Fibonacci number is " + fib(n));
    }
}
```

This code creates a dynamic programming array that stores the Fibonacci numbers up to the 'n'. BigInteger is used to handle very large numbers as the normal integer data type would overflow really quickly. The loop fills up the array using the Fibonacci sequence formula.
