Here is a simple C# program that performs an insertion sort on an array of integers:

```csharp
using System;

class Program
{
    static void InsertionSort(int[] arr)
    {
        int n = arr.Length;
        for (int i = 1; i < n; ++i)
        {
            int key = arr[i];
            int j = i - 1;

            // Move elements of arr[0..i-1], that are 
            // greater than key, to one position ahead 
            // of their current position 
            while (j >= 0 && arr[j] > key)
            {
                arr[j + 1] = arr[j];
                j = j - 1;
            }
            arr[j + 1] = key;
        }
    }

    // A utility function to print array of size n
    static void PrintArray(int[] arr)
    {
        int n = arr.Length;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)
            Console.Write(arr[i] + " ");

        Console.WriteLine();
    }

    // Driver Code 
    static void Main()
    {
        int[] arr = {3, 7, 5, 11};
        InsertionSort(arr);
        PrintArray(arr);
    }
}
```

When you run this program, it sorts the array in ascending order using the insertion sort algorithm and prints the sorted array. The output will be:

