Here is the Java code snippet that you can use to determine the perimeter of a trapezoid given the four coordinates of the points:

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double a1 = 0, b1 = 0;
        double a2 = 3, b2 = 4;
        double a3 = 7, b3 = 4;
        double a4 = 10, b4 = 0;

        double perimeter = calculatePerimeter(a1, b1, a2, b2, a3, b3, a4, b4);
        System.out.println("The perimeter of the trapezoid is: " + perimeter);
    }

    public static double calculatePerimeter(double a1, double b1, double a2, double b2, double a3, double b3, double a4, double b4) {
        double ab = distance(a1, b1, a2, b2);
        double bc = distance(a2, b2, a3, b3);
        double cd = distance(a3, b3, a4, b4);
        double da = distance(a4, b4, a1, b1);

        return ab + bc + cd + da;
    }

    public static double distance(double x1, double y1, double x2, double y2) {
        return Math.sqrt(Math.pow(x2 - x1, 2) + Math.pow(y2 - y1, 2));
    }
}
```

This code defines a function `calculatePerimeter` which takes the coordinates of the four points of the trapezoid and computes the distance between each pair of consecutive points. It then sums these distances to obtain the perimeter of the trapezoid.

