Here is an implementation in Java using Java 8 time classes. Note that in Java, week starts from Sunday which is considered as 1st day of week and Saturday as the last day.

```java
import java.time.DayOfWeek;
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.time.Month;
import java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit;
import java.time.temporal.TemporalAdjusters;

public class DateMetrics {

    public long daysBetween(LocalDate start, LocalDate end) {
        return ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(start, end);
    }

    public long weekdaysBetween(LocalDate start, LocalDate end) {
        return start.datesUntil(end)
                .filter(d -> d.getDayOfWeek().getValue() < 6 ) // 1 - Monday, .... 7 - Sunday
                .count();
    }

    public long weekendsBetween(LocalDate start, LocalDate end) {
        return start.datesUntil(end)
                .filter(d -> d.getDayOfWeek().getValue() >= 6 ) // 1 - Monday, .... 7 - Sunday
                .count();
    }

    public long specificDayBetween(DayOfWeek dayOfWeek, LocalDate start, LocalDate end) {
        return start.datesUntil(end)
                .filter(d -> d.getDayOfWeek() == dayOfWeek)
                .count();
    }

    public long specificMonthBetween(Month month, LocalDate start, LocalDate end) {
        LocalDate modifiedStart = start.withDayOfMonth(1);
        LocalDate modifiedEnd = end.with(TemporalAdjusters.lastDayOfMonth());

        return modifiedStart.datesUntil(modifiedEnd)
                .filter(d -> d.getMonth() == month && 
                     d.getDayOfMonth() == 1 && 
                     d.plusMonths(1).minusDays(1).getDayOfMonth() >= 28)
                .count();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        DateMetrics dm = new DateMetrics();
        LocalDate startDate = LocalDate.of(2020, 1, 1);
        LocalDate endDate = LocalDate.of(2021, 1, 1);

        System.out.println("Days between: " + dm.daysBetween(startDate, endDate));
        System.out.println("Weekdays between: " + dm.weekdaysBetween(startDate, endDate));
        System.out.println("Weekends between: " + dm.weekendsBetween(startDate, endDate));
        System.out.println("Mondays between: " + dm.specificDayBetween(DayOfWeek.MONDAY, startDate, endDate));
        System.out.println("Months of April: " + dm.specificMonthBetween(Month.APRIL, startDate, endDate));
    }
}
```

Please test this code thoroughly before use. Some edge cases may not be working ideally and might need minor adjustments. The time complexity is linear with respect to the number of days between given two dates. So, it should be able to handle a wide range of dates without any error or delay. 

Please note `datesUntil` method is inclusive of start date and exclusive of end date. If you want it to be inclusive of both ends, add 1 day to your end date.

