    result = is_anagram_recursive(word)
    print(f"{word} is anagram of its reversed form: {result}")
```

The function "is_anagram_recursive" checks if the first and last characters of the given word are equal. If so, it continues checking with the next characters by calling itself with the word without the first and last characters. If the characters are not equal, it returns False. Additionally, if the word is empty or has only one character, it returns True because it's an anagram of its reversed form. The code above also includes tests for the function with various examples.

