Java (solution with BigInteger class):
Java has big integer support via BigInteger. Here we need to write a bit more code.
```java
import java.math.BigInteger;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        BigInteger entity1 = new BigInteger("321");
        BigInteger entity2 = new BigInteger("456");
        BigInteger entity3 = new BigInteger("678");
        BigInteger entity4 = new BigInteger("789");

        BigInteger real = (entity1.multiply(entity3)).subtract(entity2.multiply(entity4));
        BigInteger imag = (entity1.multiply(entity4)).add(entity2.multiply(entity3));

