    }
}
```
In both of the above solutions, the time complexity for multiplication operations is around O(n^1.585) (using Karatsuba algorithm internally), where n is the number of digits. Please note that these solutions are assuming the digits are given in correct order in the input list. If the digits are reversed, the input lists need to be reversed first.

